            <ArticleTitle>Nummular headache associated with focal hair heterochromia in a child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1403-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0333102410368439</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nummular headache (NH) is a recently described headache syndrome where continuous or intermittent pain is localised to a coin-shaped region of the skull. NH can be a primary headache disorder or secondary to intracranial or extracranial pathology. We report a four-year-old boy who presented with nummular headache co-localised with a patch of discoloured hair and propose a common aetiology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
